+# Changelog
+
+## 4.2.0
+
+- `GET /prices` reads through an in-memory price cache. The database load of the shop pages drops by about 90 %.
+- New: `GET /prices/cache` shows the entries, hits, and misses of the cache.
+- Price changes from the admin page and from the supplier feed reach the cache at once.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a9cb8e1..f837631 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,3 +6,9 @@ The catalog service of the shop: products and prices.
 - `catalog/admin.py` changes single prices from the admin page.
 - `catalog/importer.py` imports the supplier price feed (up to 200 000 rows) from the admin page, in the same process.
 - `GET /prices?sku=...&sku=...` answers the shop pages, about 400 requests per second at peak.
+
+## Price cache
+
+`GET /prices` reads through `catalog/cache.py`. Each price stays in memory after its first lookup, until its price changes. The cache follows the price events of the event bus, so it has no TTL and the shop never shows an old price.
+
+`GET /prices/cache` shows the number of entries, hits, and misses.
