@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Caching in the catalog
+
+## Why
+
+At peak, `GET /prices` sends about 400 queries per second to the database, and most ask for the same 2 000 SKUs. The price cache answers them from memory.
+
+## Rules
+
+- The cache holds only known SKUs. A lookup of an unknown SKU goes to the database each time, so a new product needs no event.
+- The cache has no TTL. Each price change reaches it as an event on the in-process bus, and the cache drops that entry.
+
+## Size
+
+The catalog has about 60 000 SKUs. A cached `Price` takes about 300 bytes, so a full cache needs about 18 MB.
